<!-- HIP-YAW 10-DOF variant of bimo_biped_v2_asbuilt.xml (2026-07-23,
     morphology A/B for docs/hip-yaw-study.md). Two changes vs the as-built
     plant:
       1. A hip-yaw joint per side (yaw-first stack, Open Duck arrangement):
          a new L_hip_yaw / R_hip_yaw hinge (axis 0 0 1, range +/-45 deg,
          same joint-default class) mounted on the pelvis ABOVE the roll
          servo, carrying the unchanged roll->pitch->knee->ankle leg chain.
          The moving carrier body holds a 0.0775 kg box (carrier print + the
          roll servo, which relocates onto the carrier -- "yaw_carrier"
          segment = carrier + roll servo, 77.5 g/leg per CAD parts.py, §6);
          group 3, non-colliding. Its mass is SPRUNG on the pelvis side of
          the roll joint, so leg inertia and the swing dynamics every gait
          learned stay close. The two deck-mounted yaw servos (0.055 kg each)
          do NOT rotate with the joint -- they add to the torso; since the
          roll servos vacate the torso for the carriers, this is a
          mass-neutral swap (both 55 g), so the torso inertial is kept as-is.
          Two more position actuators (same class/gains) drive the joints.
       -- TRUE stack height 40.8 mm (YAW_STACK_DROP, CAD final 2026-07-23,
          §6): the two servos cannot nest about the shared vertical axis, so
          the second stacks in full. Standing height grows accordingly:
          torso z 0.283 -> 0.324 (+0.041 m; the earlier +0.028 was the
          optimistic study estimate). The hip-yaw joint plane lands at world
          z ~0.288 (CAD HIP_YAW_Z ~286 mm); the leg geometry BELOW the yaw
          joint is unchanged (hip-roll origin stays at world z 0.247). Envs
          derive the standing height and the joint count/layout from the
          model, so the taller 10-DOF plant works with no code literals.
       2. Torsional sole/floor friction ON (condim="4" on the class="pad"
          ground-contact geoms and the floor), same as
          bimo_biped_v2_asbuilt_torsion.xml -- both arms of the A/B run on
          the honest, twist-resisting plant.
     Masses/inertia for the carrier segment are APPROXIMATED (single box),
     pending a full inertia rollup. Everything else identical to as-built. -->
<!-- Descended from the as-built variant of bimo_biped_v2.xml (2026-07-17).
     Torso carries the tower-top accessory stack (imu_carrier + BNO055 +
     gopro_base). INERTIA, the servo blocks and (since 2026-07-30) the GROUND
     CONTACT all track the current CAD:

     - <inertial> on every body is regenerated by sim/build_v2_inertia.py from
       the current cad/stl/*.stl. Do not hand-edit them; rerun the script.
     - <geom class="servo"> boxes are the REAL case: 32.10 thick along the
       output axis, centred +1.30 toward the horn. They used to be SV_CASE_T
       (34.70) centred on zero, which is a phantom mirrored case -- the same
       one the CAD mocks carried until 2026-07-30.
     - GROUND CONTACT is now four class="pad" corner spheres per foot, sitting
       on the corners of the CAD 116 mm foot's TPU pad (106 x 46 @ x+8, i.e.
       x -45..+61, y +/-23, bottom z -17.96). It used to be one 90 x 46 @ x+10
       box, the 100 mm as-built foot. L_sole/R_sole survive as NON-COLLIDING
       reference geoms at their old pose because the envs read their geom_xpos
       (see the L_pad_* comment in L_foot for the full story, including why the
       CAD-true sole broke parity gates 2g/2h on the first attempt -- it was
       foot-ON-foot box collision, NOT box-on-plane). Standing torso z is
       unchanged at 0.3249 and stance is still four contacts per foot.
     - The two feet NO LONGER COLLIDE WITH EACH OTHER. They were the only
       self-colliding pair in the model; the leg meshes already pass through
       one another. Foot crossing is a reward-shaping matter (w_foot_cross)
       and a check_sit_pose assertion, not a contact any more.

     Foot MESH is class="cadvis", decoration only, and points at the CAD-current
     cad/stl/foot.stl; the frozen 191777e copy at cad/stl/foot_asbuilt.stl was
     deleted 2026-07-30. The rendered foot and the contact patch now agree.

     NOTE: the contact patch is therefore CAD-current, i.e. AHEAD of the robot
     on the bench until the 116 mm v3.1 feet are printed. Deliberate (user
     2026-07-30) -- the plant leads the build. Hardware evals in the interim
     are standing on a 16 mm shorter foot than the sim thinks. -->

<mujoco model="bimo_like_biped_v2">
  <!-- PROPOSED update matching the realized CAD (cad/parts.py, cad/dimensions.py).
       Differences vs bimo_biped.xml (v1):
         1. Torso center 0.280 -> 0.283 m (ankle axis is 16.9 mm above ground:
            the STS3215 lies on its side in the foot, axis at half its 24.72 mm
            width above the pocket floor; v1 assumed 14 mm).
         2. Foot sole 96 x 52 x 8 mm, center 10 mm ahead of the ankle
            (v1: 84 x 48 x 12 at +12) - matches the printed foot + TPU pad.
         3. Head geom removed: no head is built; electronics tower stays within
            the torso box envelope. Its mass is folded into the torso.
         4. Explicit masses from the CAD mass rollup + measured servo mass
            (55 g each), instead of tuned densities:
              torso 341.8 g (pelvis+tower prints, 2 roll servos, 3S LiPo 80 g,
              tower-top imu_carrier+BNO055+gopro_base 14 g,
                           driver board 20 g, wiring/screws)
              hip link 29 g (yoke_roll + yoke_pitch + screws)
              thigh/shin 79 g each (servo + leg_link + screws)
              foot 91 g (servo + foot print + TPU pad + screws)
            Total 0.879 kg (v1: 0.93 kg).
         5. Joint offsets unchanged: hip-roll -36, roll->pitch 50, thigh 90,
            shin 90 (all confirmed buildable with the real servo dimensions).
         6. CAD-true inertia: explicit <inertial> per body, computed from the
            printed-part STL meshes (cad/stl/, PLA rho*0.90) plus servo/battery/
            board boxes at their CAD positions (sim/build_v2_inertia.py; box
            geoms remain for collision/visuals, masses kept as documentation).
       Joint ranges and actuator model unchanged.
       7. CAD meshes (cad/stl/) as geoms: class "cad" parts collide with the
          floor via their convex hulls (contype 2 vs floor conaffinity 3), so
          falls, knee strikes and shin-fork grazes on bumps are physical --
          but NOT with the pads/each other (ground contact is the class="pad"
          corner spheres on the real 106 x 46 TPU pad; foot mesh is
          visual-only to avoid doubling that contact). Legacy segment boxes
          moved to group 3 (hidden, non-colliding, masses documentation-only:
          real inertia is the explicit <inertial> per body). -->
  <compiler angle="degree" autolimits="true" meshdir="../cad/stl"/>
  <option timestep="0.002" gravity="0 0 -9.81" integrator="implicitfast"/>

  <visual>
    <global offwidth="900" offheight="1100"/>
    <headlight diffuse="0.7 0.7 0.7" ambient="0.35 0.35 0.35"/>
  </visual>

  <default>
    <joint type="hinge" damping="0.6" armature="0.008" frictionloss="0.02" limited="true"/>
    <position kp="40" forcerange="-3 3"/>          <!-- STS3215 ~2.9 N*m stall -->
    <geom contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>            <!-- internal parts don't self-collide -->
    <default class="cad">
      <geom type="mesh" contype="2" conaffinity="0" group="1" rgba="0.82 0.84 0.87 1"/>
    </default>
    <default class="cadvis">
      <geom type="mesh" contype="0" conaffinity="0" group="1" rgba="0.82 0.84 0.87 1"/>
    </default>
    <default class="servo">
      <geom contype="2" conaffinity="0" group="1" rgba="0.22 0.23 0.27 1"/>
    </default>
    <!-- ground-contact primitives for the soles (2026-07-30). contype 1 vs the
         floor's conaffinity 3 -> they hit the floor; conaffinity 0 -> they do
         NOT hit each other, so the two feet no longer collide (see the
         L_pad_* block in L_foot for why). condim/friction are the old sole
         box's, so torsional sole friction is unchanged. mass 0: every body
         carries an explicit <inertial>, which is what physics uses. -->
    <default class="pad">
      <geom type="sphere" size="0.003" contype="1" conaffinity="0" mass="0"
            friction="1 0.02 0.001" condim="4" rgba="0.20 0.21 0.24 1"/>
    </default>
  </default>

  <asset>
    <!-- checker floor: the render camera tracks the torso, so an untextured
         plane makes the dash look like running in place -->
    <texture name="grid" type="2d" builtin="checker" rgb1="0.87 0.89 0.92"
             rgb2="0.77 0.80 0.85" width="512" height="512"/>
    <material name="floor_mat" texture="grid" texrepeat="24 24" texuniform="true"/>
    <mesh name="pelvis"     file="pelvis.stl"     scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
    <mesh name="tower"      file="tower.stl"      scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
    <mesh name="gopro_base" file="gopro_base.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
    <mesh name="yoke_roll"  file="yoke_roll.stl"  scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
    <mesh name="yoke_pitch" file="yoke_pitch.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
    <mesh name="leg_link"   file="leg_link.stl"   scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
    <mesh name="foot"       file="foot.stl"               scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
    <mesh name="yaw_carrier" file="yaw_carrier.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
  </asset>

  <worldbody>
    <light pos="0.6 0.4 1.5" dir="-0.4 -0.3 -1" directional="true"/>
    <geom name="floor" type="plane" size="3 3 0.1" contype="1" conaffinity="3"
          material="floor_mat" friction="1 0.02 0.001" condim="4"/>

    <body name="torso" pos="0 0 0.324">   <!-- +0.041 m: YAW_STACK_DROP 40.8 mm -->
      <freejoint/>
      <!-- 2026-07-28 board swap: TOWER_W 42->56, TOWER_H 43.5->75, board now
           upright on the +x side. Regenerate with sim/build_v2_inertia.py, do
           not hand-edit. Torso mass 341.8 -> 402.3 g (+18%) and its COM rises
           2.9 -> 14.6 mm. Fore-aft it stays balanced: the board's +x bias is
           very nearly cancelled by the pack reseating to -9.0, so COM x is
           +0.6 mm. THE PLANT HAS CHANGED -- loco_v5t was trained on the old
           torso and must at minimum be re-validated. -->
      <inertial pos="0.0010 -0.0002 0.0145" quat="0.9995 0.0108 0.0285 -0.0011" mass="0.4023" diaginertia="7.4893e-04 5.7955e-04 3.5722e-04"/>
      <!-- non-colliding visual proxy (contype/conaffinity 0, group 3); the
           explicit <inertial> above is what physics uses. x half-extent tracks
           the tower, which is now the widest thing on the torso. -->
      <geom name="torso" type="box" size="0.028 0.052 0.036" mass="0.4023" rgba="0.80 0.82 0.85 1" group="3"/>
      <geom class="cad" mesh="pelvis" pos="0 0 0.00411"/>
      <geom class="cad" mesh="tower" pos="0 0 0.00411"/>
      <geom class="cad" mesh="gopro_base" pos="0 0 0.07911"/>  <!-- tower top +31.5 mm, 2026-07-28 -->

      <geom name="servo_L_roll" class="servo" type="box" pos="0.0013 0.028 -0.02346" size="0.01605 0.01236 0.02261"/>
      <geom name="servo_R_roll" class="servo" type="box" pos="0.0013 -0.028 -0.02346" size="0.01605 0.01236 0.02261"/>
      <geom name="battery" type="box" pos="-0.009 0 0.01661" size="0.015 0.031 0.0125"
            group="1" rgba="0.16 0.30 0.55 1"/>
      <!-- IMU now lives ON the General Driver board (upright at +x): honest
           lever arm for the accelerometer. Axis rotation of the vertical
           mount is handled by deploy-time calibration + mounting-error DR. -->
      <site name="imu" pos="0.0146 0 0.0391"/>

      <!-- ================= LEFT LEG ================= -->
      <!-- hip-yaw carrier (yaw-first): vertical-axis hinge on the pelvis.
           The 0.0775 kg box is the yaw_carrier segment (carrier print + the
           roll servo, which now rides on the carrier); the 40.8 mm stack
           raises the torso but leaves the roll->ankle geometry below
           unchanged (hip-roll origin at world z 0.247). -->
      <body name="L_hip_yaw" pos="0 0.028 -0.036">
        <joint name="L_hip_yaw" axis="0 0 1" range="-45 45"/>
        <geom name="carrier_L" type="box" pos="0 0 -0.022" size="0.0125 0.0225 0.0175" mass="0.0775" group="3" rgba="0.22 0.23 0.27 1"/>
        <!-- visual-only (cadvis + mass 0: no collision/inertia change vs the
             plant the night-3 policies trained on) -- the carrier segment
             rendered as a floating gap before -->
        <geom class="cadvis" mesh="yaw_carrier" pos="0 0 -0.0029" mass="0"/>
        <geom type="box" pos="0.0013 0 -0.0285" size="0.01605 0.01236 0.02261" group="1" rgba="0.22 0.23 0.27 1" mass="0"/>
      <body name="L_hip" pos="0 0 -0.041">
        <joint name="L_hip_roll" axis="1 0 0" range="-25 25"/>
        <inertial pos="-0.0005 0.0006 -0.0220" quat="0.9503 -0.2086 0.0257 0.2299" mass="0.0296" diaginertia="1.0758e-05 1.1227e-05 1.0507e-05"/>
        <geom type="box" pos="0 0 -0.025" size="0.0175 0.0123 0.025" mass="0.029" rgba="0.22 0.23 0.27 1" group="3"/>
        <geom class="cad" mesh="yoke_roll"/>
        <geom class="cad" mesh="yoke_pitch" pos="0 0 -0.05"/>
        <body name="L_thigh" pos="0 0 -0.05">
          <joint name="L_hip_pitch" axis="0 1 0" range="-110 60"/>
        <inertial pos="-0.0010 0.0016 -0.0242" quat="0.9999 0.0031 0.0153 0.0020" mass="0.0786" diaginertia="5.5586e-05 4.8599e-05 1.6317e-05"/>
          <geom type="box" pos="0 0 -0.045" size="0.0175 0.0123 0.045" mass="0.077" rgba="0.24 0.25 0.29 1" group="3"/>
          <geom class="cad" mesh="leg_link"/>
          <geom class="servo" type="box" pos="0 0.0013 -0.0125" size="0.01236 0.01605 0.02261"/>
          <body name="L_shin" pos="0 0 -0.09">
            <joint name="L_knee" axis="0 1 0" range="-95 5"/>
        <inertial pos="-0.0010 0.0016 -0.0242" quat="0.9999 0.0031 0.0153 0.0020" mass="0.0786" diaginertia="5.5586e-05 4.8599e-05 1.6317e-05"/>
            <geom type="box" pos="0 0 -0.045" size="0.0175 0.0123 0.045" mass="0.077" rgba="0.24 0.25 0.29 1" group="3"/>
          <geom class="cad" mesh="leg_link"/>
          <geom class="servo" type="box" pos="0 0.0013 -0.0125" size="0.01236 0.01605 0.02261"/>
            <body name="L_foot" pos="0 0 -0.09">
              <joint name="L_ankle" axis="0 1 0" range="-40 40"/>
        <inertial pos="-0.0046 0.0007 -0.0063" quat="0.9979 0.0225 0.0604 -0.0063" mass="0.1104" diaginertia="2.3884e-05 9.0301e-05 9.8561e-05"/>
              <!-- GROUND CONTACT = four pad spheres at the CAD TPU-pad corners
                   (cad/dimensions.py FOOT_L 116: the 106 x 46 x 1.6 silicone
                   sheet spans x -45..+61, y +/-23, pad bottom at foot-frame z
                   -17.96 mm == ANKLE_Z). r = 3 mm with centres at z -0.015 puts
                   each sphere's lowest point at z -0.018, the plane the old box
                   stood on, so standing height is unchanged (torso z 0.3249).

                   Spheres, not one box, and no foot-foot collision. Both follow
                   from the 2026-07-30 measurement of why the CAD-true sole
                   broke parity gates 2g/2h:
                     * The break was NOT box-on-plane. Those gates are airborne
                       and CPU sees zero floor contacts in them. It was the two
                       SOLES hitting EACH OTHER: the old sole carried
                       conaffinity="1", so L_sole/R_sole were the only
                       self-colliding pair in the whole model (the class="cad"
                       leg meshes are conaffinity 0 and pass through each
                       other freely). At gate-2g t=70 the splayed, yawed
                       116 mm feet close to 0.31 mm apart; MJX's box-box
                       collider called that a penetration and CPU's did not,
                       which is the whole 9.3e-04 dqpos / 1.3e-01 dobs break.
                       conaffinity="0" on the pads retires that island of
                       self-collision; foot crossing stays governed by the
                       w_foot_cross reward and check_sit_pose's 5 mm gap test.
                     * Sphere-on-plane is ONE analytic contact point that both
                       engines agree on; MJX prunes box manifolds with a 1 mm
                       skin and drops corners CPU keeps (parity gate 3 measures
                       61% agreement on the v2 box soles). On flat ground the
                       four corner points ARE the box manifold, so settled
                       stance and its 4-contacts-per-foot solve are unchanged. -->
              <geom name="L_pad_hl" class="pad" pos="-0.045  0.023 -0.015"/>
              <geom name="L_pad_hr" class="pad" pos="-0.045 -0.023 -0.015"/>
              <geom name="L_pad_tl" class="pad" pos=" 0.061  0.023 -0.015"/>
              <geom name="L_pad_tr" class="pad" pos=" 0.061 -0.023 -0.015"/>
              <!-- REFERENCE geom, non-colliding (group 3, hidden). pos/size are
                   frozen at the old 90 x 46 @ x+10 box ON PURPOSE: walker_env /
                   env_mjx read geom_xpos["L_sole"] for the swing-foot target,
                   the CoM-over-stance kernel and the lift-clearance zero
                   (_sole_z0). Keeping it bit-identical means this change moves
                   the contact patch WITHOUT moving anything a trained policy
                   observes. Retarget it deliberately, not as a side effect. -->
              <geom name="L_sole" type="box" pos="0.010 0 -0.0140" size="0.045 0.023 0.004"
                    contype="0" conaffinity="0" group="3" mass="0.1104" rgba="0.20 0.21 0.24 1" friction="1 0.02 0.001" condim="4"/>
              <geom class="cadvis" mesh="foot" pos="0 0 -0.01636"/>
              <geom class="servo" type="box" pos="-0.0125 0.0013 0" size="0.02261 0.01605 0.01236"/>
            </body>
          </body>
        </body>
      </body>
      </body>   <!-- L_hip_yaw -->

      <!-- ================= RIGHT LEG ================= -->
      <body name="R_hip_yaw" pos="0 -0.028 -0.036">
        <joint name="R_hip_yaw" axis="0 0 1" range="-45 45"/>
        <geom name="carrier_R" type="box" pos="0 0 -0.022" size="0.0125 0.0225 0.0175" mass="0.0775" group="3" rgba="0.22 0.23 0.27 1"/>
        <!-- visual-only (cadvis + mass 0: no collision/inertia change vs the
             plant the night-3 policies trained on) -- the carrier segment
             rendered as a floating gap before -->
        <geom class="cadvis" mesh="yaw_carrier" pos="0 0 -0.0029" mass="0"/>
        <geom type="box" pos="0.0013 0 -0.0285" size="0.01605 0.01236 0.02261" group="1" rgba="0.22 0.23 0.27 1" mass="0"/>
      <body name="R_hip" pos="0 0 -0.041">
        <joint name="R_hip_roll" axis="1 0 0" range="-25 25"/>
        <inertial pos="-0.0005 0.0006 -0.0220" quat="0.9503 -0.2086 0.0257 0.2299" mass="0.0296" diaginertia="1.0758e-05 1.1227e-05 1.0507e-05"/>
        <geom type="box" pos="0 0 -0.025" size="0.0175 0.0123 0.025" mass="0.029" rgba="0.22 0.23 0.27 1" group="3"/>
        <geom class="cad" mesh="yoke_roll"/>
        <geom class="cad" mesh="yoke_pitch" pos="0 0 -0.05"/>
        <body name="R_thigh" pos="0 0 -0.05">
          <joint name="R_hip_pitch" axis="0 1 0" range="-110 60"/>
        <inertial pos="-0.0010 0.0016 -0.0242" quat="0.9999 0.0031 0.0153 0.0020" mass="0.0786" diaginertia="5.5586e-05 4.8599e-05 1.6317e-05"/>
          <geom type="box" pos="0 0 -0.045" size="0.0175 0.0123 0.045" mass="0.077" rgba="0.24 0.25 0.29 1" group="3"/>
          <geom class="cad" mesh="leg_link"/>
          <geom class="servo" type="box" pos="0 0.0013 -0.0125" size="0.01236 0.01605 0.02261"/>
          <body name="R_shin" pos="0 0 -0.09">
            <joint name="R_knee" axis="0 1 0" range="-95 5"/>
        <inertial pos="-0.0010 0.0016 -0.0242" quat="0.9999 0.0031 0.0153 0.0020" mass="0.0786" diaginertia="5.5586e-05 4.8599e-05 1.6317e-05"/>
            <geom type="box" pos="0 0 -0.045" size="0.0175 0.0123 0.045" mass="0.077" rgba="0.24 0.25 0.29 1" group="3"/>
          <geom class="cad" mesh="leg_link"/>
          <geom class="servo" type="box" pos="0 0.0013 -0.0125" size="0.01236 0.01605 0.02261"/>
            <body name="R_foot" pos="0 0 -0.09">
              <joint name="R_ankle" axis="0 1 0" range="-40 40"/>
        <inertial pos="-0.0046 0.0007 -0.0063" quat="0.9979 0.0225 0.0604 -0.0063" mass="0.1104" diaginertia="2.3884e-05 9.0301e-05 9.8561e-05"/>
              <!-- mirror of the left foot; see the L_pad_* comment above -->
              <geom name="R_pad_hl" class="pad" pos="-0.045  0.023 -0.015"/>
              <geom name="R_pad_hr" class="pad" pos="-0.045 -0.023 -0.015"/>
              <geom name="R_pad_tl" class="pad" pos=" 0.061  0.023 -0.015"/>
              <geom name="R_pad_tr" class="pad" pos=" 0.061 -0.023 -0.015"/>
              <geom name="R_sole" type="box" pos="0.010 0 -0.0140" size="0.045 0.023 0.004"
                    contype="0" conaffinity="0" group="3" mass="0.1104" rgba="0.20 0.21 0.24 1" friction="1 0.02 0.001" condim="4"/>
              <geom class="cadvis" mesh="foot" pos="0 0 -0.01636"/>
              <geom class="servo" type="box" pos="-0.0125 0.0013 0" size="0.02261 0.01605 0.01236"/>
            </body>
          </body>
        </body>
      </body>
      </body>   <!-- R_hip_yaw -->
    </body>
  </worldbody>

  <!-- actuators listed in joint-tree (qpos-address) order so the action
       vector, qpos slice and default pose all share one index layout:
       [L_yaw, L_roll, L_pitch, L_knee, L_ankle, R_yaw, R_roll, ...] -->
  <actuator>
    <position name="L_hip_yaw"   joint="L_hip_yaw"/>
    <position name="L_hip_roll"  joint="L_hip_roll"/>
    <position name="L_hip_pitch" joint="L_hip_pitch"/>
    <position name="L_knee"      joint="L_knee"/>
    <position name="L_ankle"     joint="L_ankle"/>
    <position name="R_hip_yaw"   joint="R_hip_yaw"/>
    <position name="R_hip_roll"  joint="R_hip_roll"/>
    <position name="R_hip_pitch" joint="R_hip_pitch"/>
    <position name="R_knee"      joint="R_knee"/>
    <position name="R_ankle"     joint="R_ankle"/>
  </actuator>

  <sensor>
    <framezaxis objtype="site" objname="imu" name="torso_up"/>
    <framepos   objtype="site" objname="imu" name="torso_pos"/>
  </sensor>
</mujoco>
